  "status": "Refused",
  "description": "ERECTION OF SINGLE STOREY SIDE EXTENSION FOR USE\r\nRELATED TO EXISTING PUB/RESTAURANT (CLASS E(b)).",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:115%&quot;&gt;The\r\nproposed development, by reason of the absence of sufficient information\r\nrelating to capacity, trip generation, parking demand and parking management,\r\nfails to demonstrate that adequate parking provision can be made for the\r\ndevelopment and that the proposal would not result in unacceptable pressure on\r\nsurrounding roads&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;to the detriment of highway safety, pedestrian\r\nsafety and the free flow of traffic. The proposal is therefore contrary to\r\nPolicies TR3, TR4 and TR6 of the National Planning Policy Framework (2026),\r\nPolicies T1, T4, T6 and T7 of the London Plan (2021), and Policies T16.3 and\r\nT16.4 of the Merton Local Plan (2024).&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;line-height:115%&quot;&gt;The applicant has failed to provide\r\nsufficient information to demonstrate that the Biodiversity Gain Hierarchy has\r\nbeen appropriately applied relating to off-site biodiversity units. The proposal\r\nfails to comply with the Environment Act 2021, Policy N2 of the National\r\nPlanning Policy Framework (2026) and Policy O15.3 of the Merton Local Plan\r\n(2024).&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoListParagraph&quot; style=&quot;margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: 15pt;&quot;&gt;By reason of the absence of a\r\nNoise Impact Assessment or sufficient information regarding the existing and\r\nproposed operation of the site, and having regard to the sensitivity of the\r\nsurrounding area and the site&#x27;s established history, the Local Planning\r\nAuthority cannot be satisfied that the proposed development would not result in\r\nunacceptable noise and disturbance impacts to neighbouring occupiers. The\r\nproposal therefore fails to demonstrate compliance with Policy P3 of the National\r\nPlanning Policy Framework (2026), Policy D14 of the London Plan (2021) and\r\nPolicy P15.10 of the Merton Local Plan (2024).&lt;font face=&quot;Segoe UI, sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10.5pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
